---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Programmes from '../components/Programmes.astro';
import { location, sectors, programmes, partnerNetwork, startupProgramme } from '../facts';

// Copy repris de about.html, nettoyé.
// Ce qui a été retiré et pourquoi est dans docs/REVIEW.md, section « Retiré »,
// avec la ligne de restauration de chaque passage.
//
// 2026-10-09 : la section partenariat n'attend plus une URL publique pour
// s'afficher. Elle cite les deux programmes Anthropic (Karim : « show both
// together … and on About »), avec leurs statuts tirés de facts.ts. La
// description du Claude Partner Network est celle de la page d'annonce
// d'Anthropic (partnerNetwork.value.description dans facts.ts).
---

<Base
  title="About Syntexia"
  description="Syntexia builds automation and voice systems that run inside the tools a company already uses."
  path="/about"
>
  <section class="section first">
    <div class="shell">
      <h1>The era of generic AI is ending. What comes next runs inside the business.</h1>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Most organisations do not need another general-purpose model with a clever
          prompt. They need intelligence that lives where the work happens: in the inbox,
          the phone line, the CRM, the accounting system, the operations stack.
        </p>
        <p>
          Syntexia is built on a single idea. Real intelligence is embedded, not bolted
          on. It reads the same documents your team reads. It picks up the phone. It
          writes the report. It catches the discrepancy before it becomes a problem.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are not selling a platform staff have to learn. We are building the
          intelligence layer for serious operations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>The work is methodical.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          We start by mapping the systems already in use, the questions teams are already
          asking, the operations that consume their time. Then we embed intelligence into
          that fabric, quietly, without asking anyone to learn a new tool.
        </p>
        <p>
          Anything uncertain is flagged with its reason, and a person decides. Each
          organisation gets its own deployment, with its own rules and its own templates.
          We reuse the architecture between clients. We never reuse the data.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {programmes.length > 0 && (
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="claude-title">
      <div class="shell">
        <h2 id="claude-title">We build with Claude</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          {partnerNetwork && (
            <p>
              Syntexia is a {partnerNetwork.value.tier} in the {partnerNetwork.value.programme},{' '}
              {partnerNetwork.value.description}{startupProgramme ? <>, and a member of {startupProgramme.value.name}</> : null}.
            </p>
          )}
          <p>
            Claude is the model family we believe sets the standard for the kind of careful,
            high-stakes work our customers operate in. The models change. What does not
            change is that a person makes the decision.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="progs">
          <Programmes variant="register" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>What we build for</h2>
      <div class="sectors">
        {sectors.map((s) => (
          <div class="sector">
            <h3>{s.name}</h3>
            <p>{s.blurb}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section on-black">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Where</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        {location && <p class="where">{location.value}</p>}
        <p>
          We work where the regulation is serious, where the operations are real, and
          where the cost of being wrong is high. That is the standard we build to.
        </p>
        
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>The team</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p><a href="/team">See who builds it</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .first { border-top: 0; }
  .prose { margin-top: var(--s-6); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--s-5); }
  .where { font-size: 19px; color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }
  .progs { margin-top: var(--s-8); }
  .sectors {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--s-7);
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
  }
  .sector { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: var(--s-5); }
  .sector p { margin-top: var(--s-3); }
</style>
